---
// DRAFT — matches how the licence actually works, but needs a legal review and
// the real company number/address before launch.
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import { SITE, PRICE, PRODUCT } from "../../consts";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../../lib/schema";

const crumbs = [
	{ label: "Home", href: "/" },
	{ label: "Terms", href: "/legal/terms/" },
];
const UPDATED = "26 July 2026";
---

<Page
	title="Terms of sale and licence"
	heading="Terms"
	description={`The licence terms for ${SITE.name}: what you may do with the software, what one licence covers, and the limits of our liability.`}
	intro={`Last updated ${UPDATED}. These terms apply when you buy or use ${SITE.name}.`}
	eyebrow="Legal"
	crumbs={crumbs}
	schema={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}
	cta={false}
	narrow
>
	<section class="pt-0">
		<div class="wrap wrap-narrow prose">
			<h2>1. The licence</h2>
			<p>
				Buying {SITE.name} grants you a perpetual, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to
				use the software on one computer. {PRODUCT.licence}. You may move the licence between
				computers by releasing it from the old one first.
			</p>

			<h2>2. What you may not do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Share, resell, rent or publish the application files or your licence key.</li>
				<li>Run one licence on more than one computer at a time.</li>
				<li>Reverse engineer, decompile or modify the software, except where law permits it regardless of contract.</li>
				<li>Circumvent or tamper with licence activation.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>A licence found in use on multiple machines may be suspended without refund.</p>

			<h2>3. Your content and your responsibility</h2>
			<p>
				You are responsible for having the right to process any video you put through the
				software. {SITE.name} is a tool for repurposing material you own or are authorised to
				edit. It is not a means of copying other people's work, and using it that way breaches
				these terms as well as the rights of whoever owns the material.
			</p>

			<h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
			<p>
				AI features require your own Google Gemini API key and are subject to Google's terms
				and pricing. We are not responsible for their availability, their output, or charges
				you incur with them. If a third-party platform changes in a way that breaks a feature,
				we will fix it where we reasonably can, but we cannot guarantee any external service
				will continue to work.
			</p>

			<h2>5. Price and payment</h2>
			<p>
				The price is {PRICE.display} ({PRICE.currency}), charged once, processed by Stripe.
				Applicable taxes are added at checkout where required.
			</p>

			<h2>6. Refunds</h2>
			<p>
				Fourteen days from purchase, no reason required — see the
				<a href="/legal/refund/">refund policy</a>. Refunded licences are deactivated.
			</p>

			<h2>7. Updates</h2>
			<p>
				Updates to the version you purchased are included. A future major version may be
				offered as a paid upgrade; the version you bought continues to work regardless.
			</p>

			<h2>8. Warranty and liability</h2>
			<p>
				The software is provided as it is. We do not warrant that it will be uninterrupted or
				error-free, or that AI output will be accurate or suitable for any particular purpose —
				always review clips before publishing them. To the extent permitted by law, our total
				liability is limited to the amount you paid. Nothing here limits liability for death,
				personal injury or fraud, and nothing affects your statutory rights as a consumer.
			</p>

			<h2>9. Governing law</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and the courts of England
				and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.
			</p>

			<h2>10. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE.company}, {SITE.companyCountry} —
				<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Page>

<style>
	.pt-0 {
		padding-top: 8px;
	}
</style>
